> expand (x + 1/2)^2
  ucas: expand (x + 1/2)^2
expand (x + 0.5)^2
  = x^2 + x + 1/4
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> factor x^2 + x/2 + 1/4
  ucas: factor x^2 + x/2 + 1/4
factor x^2 + x/2 + 0.25
  = (4x^2 + 2x + 1)/4
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> gcd x^2 - 1/4, x - 1/2
gcd x^2 - 0.25, x - 0.5
  = 2x - 1
  check: it divides both exactly, and the cofactors are coprime
  (normalized: integer coefficients without a common factor, leading coefficient positive)
> lcm x^2 - 1/4, x - 1/2
lcm x^2 - 0.25, x - 0.5
  = (2x - 1)*(2x + 1)
    = 4x^2 - 1
  check: both divide it exactly
> quo x, 3
quo x, 3
  = x/3
  (in x: P = Q*quotient + remainder, deg remainder < 0)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> rem x^2 + 1/2, x + 1/2
rem x^2 + 0.5, x + 0.5
  = 3/4
  (in x: P = Q*quotient + remainder, deg remainder < 1)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> discriminant x^2 + x + 1/4
discriminant x^2 + x + 0.25
  in x (degree 2): 0
  = 0: a repeated root
  check: lc^(2n-2) * product of (ri - rj)^2 over the roots = 0 (agrees)
> resultant 2x - 1, x^2 + 1
resultant 2x - 1, x^2 + 1
  in x: 5
  nonzero: no common root
  check: lc(P)^deg(Q) * product of Q over the roots of P = 5 (agrees)
> collect x*y + x*z + 2x + 2y in x
collect x*y + x*z + 2x + 2y
  = (y + z + 2)*x + 2y
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
